  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Jelly on the Desk",
    "overview": "A calm, well-lit study desk with one irresistible object on it: a glossy raspberry jelly with the word \"polyra\" on it. The jelly is alive. It breathes, shifts shape, squashes under the finger and starts the day's session. Everything else on the desk is tidy and quiet: soft blush paper, white cards, aubergine ink, generous corners. The fun lives in one place so the rest of the app can stay serious about learning without ever feeling childish.\n\nThe audience is Persian-speaking adults who study in short daily gaps on a phone. The interface is right-to-left Persian by default and must flip cleanly to left-to-right for other interface languages. French and German text is always set in a soft serif so the language being learned looks like a beautiful book, not a game. Density is low on the learner's daily loop: one decision per screen, big targets, the answer area at the thumb.\n\nThe owner rejected three earlier worlds: flat geometry (childish), the engraved certificate and Tehran modernism. The owner then fixed the palette to six colors and asked for the jelly Start button. Treat both as permanent.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Six brand colors only; every other value is a tint, shade or wash of one of them.",
      "One living material (the jelly). It appears on Start and, small and still, on the station drop.",
      "Persian in Vazirmatn, the target language in Fraunces with its SOFT axis turned up.",
      "Day and night designed separately; night is aubergine, not grey.",
      "Soft, tinted shadows and generous radii (20 to 28px); no hard edges, no hard offset shadows.",
      "Sound, light haptics and spring motion on every touch, all switchable, all reduced-motion aware."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Six Colors Rule",
        "body": "The owner's six colors (#D81E5B, #A8134A, #F0527F, #FDE7EF, #2B1020, #1FB5A8) are the whole brand. New values are only tints, shades or washes of these, plus the three gender colors.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Teal Means Right Rule",
        "body": "Teal appears only for correct answers and protection (the streak freeze). Never as decoration, never as a link color.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wrong Is Not Red Rule",
        "body": "A wrong answer is deep raspberry (#A8134A) with a wash, never a pure red and never shaking the whole screen. Mistakes are part of learning (PRD: the first attempt is never penalized).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Persian is always Vazirmatn, the language being learned is always Fraunces. Latin text is isolated (`direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: isolate`) so it never scrambles inside a Persian line.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Uppercase Rule",
        "body": "No uppercase eyebrows, no letter-spaced kicker labels above headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Living Thing Rule",
        "body": "Only the jelly moves on its own. Everything else moves only in response to a touch or a state change.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Is Furniture Rule",
        "body": "Blur is used only for bars that content scrolls under (top bar, session bar, bottom action block). No decorative glass cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every color inside the six brand colors, their tints and washes, plus the three gender colors.",
      "**Do** use teal only for \"right\" and the streak freeze, and deep raspberry (#A8134A) for \"wrong\".",
      "**Do** set the language being learned in Fraunces SOFT and isolate it as left-to-right text.",
      "**Do** design night separately: aubergine ground (#2B1020), #381A2B surfaces, lighter text tints.",
      "**Do** give every touch a response: a short squash or spring, a soft sound and a light buzz, each switchable in settings and silent under reduced motion.",
      "**Do** keep touch targets at 44px or more, and the main action in the bottom block at the thumb.",
      "**Do** self-host Vazirmatn and Fraunces in the app; prototypes may use Google Fonts only as previews."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a second living or self-moving element next to the jelly; the rest of the screen stays calm.",
      "**Don't** write «شروع» on the jelly or replace it with a regular button.",
      "**Don't** use emoji, mascots, confetti, XP, leagues or badges (PRD §1, §2).",
      "**Don't** return to the rejected worlds: flat geometric skill shapes, engraved certificate paper, Tehran modernism, or a cool grey and cobalt \"business\" palette.",
      "**Don't** use gradient text anywhere except the jelly wordmark.",
      "**Don't** use uppercase eyebrows, hard offset shadows, or decorative glass cards.",
